## Why GPL-3.0

The on-device speech runtime, sherpa-onnx, statically links espeak-ng, which is
GPL-3.0. Distributing that combination makes the combined work GPL-3.0, so the
app is GPL-3.0 as a whole rather than Apache-2.0 with an undeclared GPL
component inside it.

## Third-party components in the build

  - sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa) — Apache-2.0
  - espeak-ng (the fork used by sherpa-onnx) — GPL-3.0
  - ONNX Runtime (Microsoft) — MIT
  - Hermes Agent client protocol and documentation (Nous Research)

